Example of PHP code for data scientists:
```
<?php
// Load the data from a CSV file
$data = array_map('str_getcsv', file('data.csv'));
// Compute the mean of a column
$column = array_column($data, 'age');
$mean = array_sum($column) / count($column);
echo "Mean age: $mean\n";
// Compute the correlation between two columns
$column1 = array_column($data, 'age');
$column2 = array_column($data, 'income');
$correlation = corr($column1, $column2);
echo "Correlation: $correlation\n";
// Define the correlation function
function corr($x, $y) {
    $n = count($x);
    $mean_x = array_sum($x) / $n;
    $mean_y = array_sum($y) / $n;
    $stddev_x = sqrt(array_sum(array_map(function($xi) use ($mean_x) { return pow($xi - $mean_x, 2); }, $x)) / $n);
    $stddev_y = sqrt(array_sum(array_map(function($yi) use ($mean_y) { return pow($yi - $mean_y, 2); }, $y)) / $n);
    $covariance = array_sum(array_map(function($xi, $yi) use ($mean_x, $mean_y) { return ($xi - $mean_x) * ($yi - $mean_y); }, $x, $y)) / $n;
    return $covariance / ($stddev_x * $stddev_y);
}
?>
```
