1. Gather restaurant data: Use an API such as Yelp or Google Places to gather restaurant data such as location, cuisine, price range, ambiance, and noise level. You can also use a database to store this information.
2. Filter restaurants based on dietary requirements: Use a filter to remove restaurants that do not cater to specific dietary requirements such as vegetarian, vegan, or gluten-free.
3. Filter restaurants based on party size: Use a filter to remove restaurants that cannot accommodate the party size.
4. Filter restaurants based on ambiance and noise level: Use a filter to remove restaurants that do not match the desired ambiance and noise level.
5. Sort restaurants based on cost-effectiveness and positive past reviews and ratings: Use a sorting algorithm to rank restaurants based on cost-effectiveness and positive past reviews and ratings.
6. Display information on private dining areas: Use the restaurant data or API to display information on the availability of private dining areas for the group.
Here is an example of a JavaScript function that could help achieve this functionality:
```
function recommendRestaurant(dietaryRequirements, partySize, ambiance, noiseLevel) {
  // gather restaurant data
  const restaurants = getRestaurants();
  // filter restaurants based on dietary requirements
  const filteredRestaurants = restaurants.filter(restaurant => {
    return restaurant.dietaryRequirements.includes(dietaryRequirements);
  });
  // filter restaurants based on party size
  const partySizeRestaurants = filteredRestaurants.filter(restaurant => {
    return restaurant.partySize >= partySize;
  });
  // filter restaurants based on ambiance and noise level
  const ambianceRestaurants = partySizeRestaurants.filter(restaurant => {
    return restaurant.ambiance === ambiance && restaurant.noiseLevel === noiseLevel;
  });
  // sort restaurants based on cost-effectiveness and positive past reviews and ratings
  const sortedRestaurants = ambianceRestaurants.sort((a, b) => {
    return a.costEffectiveness - b.costEffectiveness || b.reviews - a.reviews;
  });
  // display information on private dining areas
  const privateDiningAreas = sortedRestaurants.map(restaurant => {
    return restaurant.privateDiningAreas;
  });
  return sortedRestaurants[0];
}
```

